Package: shinyasync
Title: Async Shiny Reactives on 'mirai'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Dawie", "Griesel", , "dawiegr@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Move slow work off the 'Shiny' session thread without changing
    how you write 'Shiny'. Provides asynchronous counterparts of reactive(),
    observe() and reactiveVal() that evaluate their expressions on 'mirai'
    daemons, track reactive dependencies, cancel superseded work and return
    the previous value while a new one is computed.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://dawiegriesel.github.io/shinyasync/, https://github.com/dawiegriesel/shinyasync
BugReports: https://github.com/dawiegriesel/shinyasync/issues
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports: 
    codetools,
    later,
    mirai (>= 2.0.0),
    parallel,
    promises,
    shiny (>= 1.8.1)
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
